# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How to use
# 1) Copy this file to `.env` (e.g., backend/.env).
# 2) Fill in the blanks.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# === PostgreSQL (Neon) ========================================================
# The target is explicit and has NO default. A bare DATABASE_URL is the variable
# every tool and stray script picks up without being told to, and on this
# project that bare name pointed at the database everything had been writing to
# for weeks. `RISK_DB_TARGET` must say which database is meant; `util/db.py`
# resolves it, and every command prints the target and the database it reached
# before doing any work.
#
#   dev  -> DEV_DATABASE_URL
#   prod -> PROD_DATABASE_URL
#
# Asking for a target whose variable is empty fails loudly and names it.
RISK_DB_TARGET='dev'

# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME?sslmode=require
DEV_DATABASE_URL=''

# There is no production database yet. Leave this blank until there is one;
# nothing should be able to reach production by accident.
PROD_DATABASE_URL=''

# === OpenAI ===================================================================
# Key usually starts with "sk-". Do NOT expose via NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
OPENAI_API_KEY=''

# === Crawlbase ================================================================
# Server-side token for Crawlbase REST API (advanced scraper).
CRAWLBASE_TOKEN=''

# Optional: client-side token for the Crawlbase JS snippet
CRAWLBASE_JS_TOKEN=''

# === FMP (Financial Modeling Prep) ============================================
# API key for the economic-calendar feed (Econ Calendar pane) AND the live
# Prices feed (main.py prices: batch-quote, historical-price-eod, and
# treasury-rates endpoints). Plan must include those endpoints. The prices
# loop reuses this key and the database target above — no other secret is needed.
FMP_API_KEY=''
